[[File:Fighting Hell-Rat Behemoth.png|thumb|306x306px|A hell cat and a Hell-Rat Behemoth face off.{{Map:Spicy stew spices}}]]
The player can give their cat [[fish]] or [[Bucket of milk|milk]] to heal them by using them on the curtain or on the cat directly. Since all food given to your cat heal for the same amount, [[raw karambwanji]] is the best type of food, allowing to obtain multiple spices without having to bank. It is highly recommended that players use [[wily cat]]s to kill Hell-Rat Behemoths as they can kill them quickly and efficiently. If the cat dies during the fight, it is permanently lost and players will have to obtain another kitten from [[Gertrude]]. It should be noted players can also use overgrown cats to fight in the instance.

When successfully defeated, the player will exit the instance and will automatically be given the four-dosed spice that the Behemoth was guarding. If the player's inventory is full, it will be dropped on the floor right under the player.

If a player is assigned to kill rats as a Slayer task, defeating a Hell-rat Behemoth will count as a kill towards the task and award 15 Slayer experience.

